# The store, and this is the line that matters.
#
# The default store is `maer-sync.sqlite` in the working directory, so
# whoever follows the setup guide inside a clone creates one HERE. It holds
# scrypt hashes of account secrets and digests of live tokens. Nothing else
# in this repository would stop a `git add -A` from committing it.
#
# In the app repository this line read `SyncService/*.sqlite`, scoped to the
# directory the service used to live in. That scope came along with the move
# and left nothing behind, so the pattern had to be written again here rather
# than being inherited. It was missing for the length of one branch, and the
# 25 compiled files that branch carried are what made it visible.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Compiled bytecode. Harmless in itself, and the reason the missing store
# line was noticed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The setup guide creates this inside the clone.
.venv/
